    bottomLine: "The folding pick for runners and hikers who want both halves of a hill, at about half the price of NordicTrack’s touchscreen Commercial models.",
    description: "The Commercial LE is NordicTrack’s Commercial-series frame without the big screen, and that is what makes it the value route to decline on a folding treadmill. The Amazon listing gives a range from a -3% decline to a 12% incline, speeds from 0 to 12 mph, RunFlex cushioning, a 7-inch LCD for live stats and a device shelf, and a folding frame that lowers itself to the floor when you press the foot bar. With an iFIT membership your phone or tablet runs trainer and route workouts that move the speed and grade for you, including into decline; without one, you set speed and incline from the console yourself. Several retailers list the same -3% to 12% range and the foot-bar fold (checked November 2026). We have kept the motor rating and capacity off the spec line because retailers quote them inconsistently (one uses horsepower, another continuous horsepower) and the Amazon listing gives neither; check the manual for the maximum user weight before ordering if you are near the top of a typical range. For more on what -3% is good for, see our guide to treadmills with decline. Amazon listed it at $1,299 on 21 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "therun-16-folding-incline-treadmill",
    name: "THERUN 16% Folding Incline Treadmill",
    brand: "THERUN",
    category: "Steep auto incline under $500 with stated folded size",
    badge: "Best Under $500",
