    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41HAdIkHr8L._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $450 (Amazon, 21 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":450,"high":450},
    specs: "0-16% auto incline (16 levels) · 0.6-10 mph · 17 x 47.2 in. belt · hydraulic folding · 29.5 x 31.1 x 54.7 in. folded · about 400 lb capacity",
    pros: [
      "16% powered incline, steeper than any of the branded full-size picks",
      "Folded dimensions are stated on the listing, so you can measure your spot",
      "Hydraulic folding and transport wheels",
      "Arrives mostly assembled, per the listing",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A 47.2-inch belt suits walking and jogging more than long running strides",
      "The listing describes capacity as “about 400 lbs”, which is vaguer than a rated figure",
      "App and console are basic compared with the NordicTrack picks",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The cheapest way to get a genuinely steep powered climb on a treadmill that folds upright, as long as you mostly walk.",
    description: "THERUN sells several incline treadmills on Amazon; this is the 16% model with hydraulic folding, a different machine from the 20% THERUN on our auto incline page. The listing gives 16 incline levels from 0% to 16%, speeds from 0.6 to 10 mph, a 47.2 by 17-inch running surface with ten shock absorbers, a Bluetooth app connection, shortcut buttons for speed and incline, two cup holders and a frame that bears “about 400 lbs”. It is also the most useful listing here for a small room, because it states the folded size: 29.5 by 31.1 by 54.7 inches. That puts the folded footprint at well under seven square feet, and the 54.7-inch height clears most window sills and shelves. The listing says it arrives mostly assembled and sets up in under 20 minutes. It describes a 4.0 HP motor and a separate incline motor; we have not put the horsepower on the card because unbranded peak ratings are not comparable across makers. Sixteen per cent is about 9 degrees, which is a real hiking grade. The trade is deck length: at 47.2 inches, it is right for incline walking and easy jogging, and short for fast running. Amazon listed it at $449.98 on 21 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "nordictrack-t-series-16",
    name: "NordicTrack T Series 16",
    brand: "NordicTrack",
    category: "Folding incline treadmill with a large touchscreen",
    badge: "Best Touchscreen",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FBYJPXQ9?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31IJMmHM8RL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":491},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $1,299 (Amazon, 21 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":1299,"high":1299},
    specs: "0-12% incline · 0-12 mph · 16 in. tilting touchscreen · SelectFlex adjustable cushioning · folding with assisted lowering",
    pros: [
      "A 16-inch touchscreen that tilts for your height",
      "0-12% incline and 12 mph for running as well as walking",
      "Cushioning adjusts from soft to firm",
      "Foot-bar assisted lowering, as on the Commercial LE",
