            percentage or a clear range, not just “incline” in the title. Third, the brand had to be
            named and the listing had to give enough figures to build an honest card. A few
            otherwise plausible machines failed the last test: one well-known folding treadmill’s
            listing had a single feature bullet, and a NordicTrack starter model gave a clear incline
            range but did not say in its bullets that it folds, so we left both out rather than fill
            the gaps from memory.
          </p>
          <p>
            Among the machines that passed, we picked for genuinely different buyers rather than six
            versions of the same treadmill: a best all-rounder, decline, steep incline on a budget, a
            touchscreen, the steepest grade, and the cheapest real incline. Prices are what Amazon
            showed on 21 November 2026 and move often, especially in the run-up to <a href="/treadmill-black-friday-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Black Friday</a>.
          </p>
